IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rta-types`
IMPORT `rta-dates`
IMPORT `rta-application`
IMPORT `rta-money`
IMPORT `rta-termination`
IMPORT `rta-entry`
IMPORT `rta-tribunal`

-- Residential Tenancies Act 1986 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this tenancy step (a notice to terminate, a rent increase, a bond, a
--    demand for rent in advance, an entry, a boarding house termination, or
--    an application about an unlawful act), does the Act apply, is the step
--    lawful, and on what date does it take effect or must it be made by?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Tenancy step` IS ONE OF
    `a notice to terminate`         HAS `the termination notice`      IS A `Termination notice`
    `a rent increase`               HAS `the rent increase notice`    IS A `Rent increase notice`
    `a bond demand`                 HAS `the bond demand`             IS A `Bond demand`
    `a demand for rent in advance`  HAS `the rent demand`             IS A `Rent demand`
    `an entry on notice`            HAS `the entry notice`            IS AN `Entry notice`
    `a boarding house termination`  HAS `the boarding house notice`   IS A `Boarding house notice`
    `an unlawful act application`   HAS `the unlawful act application` IS AN `Unlawful act application`

DECLARE `Step answer` HAS
    `the Act applies`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the step is lawful`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    -- the earliest day a notice to terminate may require vacating; the
    -- earliest day a rent increase may take effect; the last day to apply
    -- about an unlawful act. NOTHING for the other steps, or where no day
    -- applies.
    `the key date`                                      IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref ss 5, 8, 18-24, 48, 50-51, 53-59B, 66U-66V, 109, 136, 136A
@export default For one step in a New Zealand residential tenancy, under the Residential Tenancies Act 1986: whether the Act applies to the tenancy (s 5, s 8); whether the step is lawful — a notice to terminate (ss 50-59B with the s 136 deemed service and s 136A periods), a rent increase (s 24), a bond (ss 18-18A), rent in advance (s 23), an entry on notice (s 48), a boarding house termination (ss 66U-66V), or an application about an unlawful act (s 109, in time); and the key date — the earliest date to vacate, the earliest date a rent increase may take effect, or the last day to apply about the unlawful act. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A Tenancy  @desc Which s 5 exclusion applies (if any), any written agreement that the Act applies, and the length of any fixed term
      step IS A `Tenancy step`  @desc The step and its facts
      cal IS A `Local calendar`  @desc The Matariki Observance Days and local anniversary days, for working days
GIVETH A `Step answer`
`the tenancy step answer for` t `, step` step `, calendar` cal MEANS
    `Step answer` WITH
        `the Act applies`       IS applies
        `the step is lawful`    IS applies AND lawful
        `the key date`          IS IF applies THEN date ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        applies MEANS `the Act applies to` t
        lawful MEANS
            CONSIDER step
            WHEN `a notice to terminate` n THEN
                    `the termination notice is lawful` n cal
                AND ((NOT isSection51 (n's `ground`)) OR `sections 25 to 28 and 51 apply to` t)
            WHEN `a rent increase` n THEN `the rent increase is lawful` n
            WHEN `a bond demand` b THEN `the landlord may require the bond` b
            WHEN `a demand for rent in advance` r THEN `the landlord may require the rent in advance` r
            WHEN `an entry on notice` e THEN `the landlord may enter` e
            WHEN `a boarding house termination` n THEN `the boarding house termination is lawful` n
            WHEN `an unlawful act application` a THEN `the unlawful act application is in time` a
        date MEANS
            CONSIDER step
            WHEN `a notice to terminate` n THEN `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` n `, calendar` cal
            WHEN `a rent increase` n THEN JUST (`the earliest day the increase may take effect, notice` n)
            WHEN `an unlawful act application` a THEN `the last day to apply about the unlawful act` a
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
        GIVEN g IS A `Ground for notice`
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        isSection51 g MEANS
               g EQUALS `s 51(1) the landlord, in any case`
            OR g EQUALS `s 51(2)(a) the owner or family will live there`
            OR g EQUALS `s 51(2)(b) an unconditional sale needs vacant possession`
            OR g EQUALS `s 51(2)(c) required for employees or contractors, as stated in the agreement`
            OR g EQUALS `s 51(2)(d) required for school board employees or contractors (the Crown), as stated in the agreement`
            OR g EQUALS `s 51(2A) the tenant, in any case`
